course: dictionary
lesson: 5530
title: A ledge is a narrow shelf
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A ledge is a narrow, flat shelf that sticks out from a wall, a cliff or a window. When you meet the word, look at the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «They find the Mock Turtle sitting sad and lonely on a ledge of rock.» You can sit on a ledge, and it is flat and sticks out, so a ledge must be a flat shelf of rock.
explain: Look for clues in other sentences too. «City pigeons are descended from wild rock doves that nest on sea cliffs, and ledges on tall buildings are like cliffs to them.» The ledges are compared to cliffs, so they are high, steep places where birds can rest and nest. Always ask: what could fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: A window ledge is the shelf at the bottom of a window, also called a windowsill. Plants often sit on a window ledge in the sun. Ledges can be very high, so they can be dangerous. «Quarry water is very cold and deep and has hidden machinery and ledges, and people drown in it every summer.» Never climb onto a ledge, and never lean out of a window to reach one.
fact: A ledge is a narrow, flat shelf sticking out from a wall, cliff or window.
fact: A window ledge is another name for a windowsill, the shelf at the bottom of a window.
fact: «Ledges on tall buildings are like cliffs to them» means city pigeons use high ledges as places to rest and nest.
fact: «They find the Mock Turtle sitting sad and lonely on a ledge of rock.» Here a ledge is a flat place of rock to sit on.
fact: Do not climb onto ledges or lean out of windows, because a fall can cause serious injury.
exercise: «They find the Mock Turtle sitting sad and lonely on a ledge of rock.» What is a ledge here? | A deep hole in the ground | A soft bed of grass | A loud noise | *A narrow, flat shelf of rock
exercise: What is a window ledge? | The door at the side of a house | The curtain that hangs by a window | The glass in the middle of a window | *The shelf at the bottom of a window
exercise: Find and copy one word from «ledges on tall buildings are like cliffs to them» that means a high, steep rock face. | buildings | *cliffs | tall | ledges
test: Why must you not climb onto a ledge? | *Because you could fall and get badly hurt | Because ledges are made of soft cake | Because ledges are always warm and dry | Because it is a fun game for everyone
test: Which of these is a ledge? | A wide, open field | A tall tree in a park | *A flat shelf sticking out from a cliff | A cup of hot tea
exam: Which sentence uses ledge to mean a shelf? | *Mum put the plant on the window ledge, where the sun shines | Mum read the book under the old oak tree | Mum ran along the long, dark road | Mum put the plant in the deep end of the pool
